<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36721" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plūmĕus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>downy</i>, <i>covered</i> or <i>filled with
			down</i>, <i>down-</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">culcita plumea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 3, 19, 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aures,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 23, 33, § 68</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Downy</i>, <i>like down</i>, i. e.
				<i>light</i>, <i>soft</i>, <i>delicate</i> (<b>poet.</b> and
			post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plumea pondera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					4, 19, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nives,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plumea et lactea cutis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 135, 26</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Embroidered</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indumenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 295</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
